  Duty:   credit "Forecast data: NOAA HRRR via NOAA Open Data Dissemination".

US government geographic facts used in viewpoints/manifests/ and plates/specs/
  USGS 3DEP elevations (Elevation Point Query Service), USGS GNIS place
  coordinates, the NPS ARD webcams feature layer (ArcGIS), and EPA AirNow and
  CASTNET site coordinates.
  Basis:  US government works, public domain. Only coordinates and heights
          are used; each manifest and plate spec lists its sources with access
          dates.

USGS 3DEP bare-earth elevation model (raster), used by plates/
  A subset exported as a float32 GeoTIFF by the National Map's
  3DEPElevation ImageServer (exportImage), for the plate builder's skyline,
  ray cast and landmark-band masks (PRD §8.5).
  Basis:  US government work, public domain.
  Status: the subsets stay in the data dir; the plate manifest records each
          request and its SHA-256. None is in this repository.

Bright Star Catalogue, 5th revised edition (Hoffleit & Warren 1991; CDS V/50)
  Read by plates/ (starmatch.py) from the owner's own local copy, to match
  stars in night frames for the camera pose (PRD §8.5).
  Status: its terms of use are still to be confirmed by the owner. Nothing of
          the catalogue is in this repository; the match files, which hold
          catalogue positions, stay in the data dir.

Other cited sources in the manifests
  TopoQuest and Wikipedia are cited for single facts (a GNIS id, a summit
